 r"I am writing to apply for the Associate Consultant position on Konrad's Strategy team in London. I have completed an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London, where a distinction is expected, after graduating from Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. Across my academic and professional experience, I have worked on understanding what a client actually needs, defining what a good outcome looks like, and turning analysis into a recommendation someone could act on. I am particularly interested in this role because it combines business strategy with AI and digital products that real people use.",

 r"What attracts me most to Konrad is that the strategy work has a visible end point: a product or experience that is designed and built with the client, not just a report. I enjoy taking an unclear business problem, identifying what users actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved. The posting describes working alongside Design and Technology teams, running workshops and tracking how AI is changing products, and that is the kind of consulting I want to do.",

 r"In my current role at TikTok Shop UK, I analyse merchant and transaction data in SQL and Python and build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track initiatives. When my supervisor asked me to configure a merchant campaign by hand, I saw the logic after a few examples and proposed building an AI agent with Claude Code, with a validation step to check its accuracy. My supervisor was sceptical at first, so I explained what the agent would do and how we would check its output, and I delivered it before the deadline. It cut the time the task took by around 40 to 50 percent. This experience taught me that a new tool is only adopted once the person who owns the problem trusts how it works.",

 r"At DS Digital Technology, I worked as a Data Scientist Intern on a patient-facing AI product for a pharmaceutical client. With the client's clinical experts, I designed a 246-question benchmark and a scoring rubric that became the client's acceptance standard, compared six LLM providers across more than 2,400 responses, and designed blinded A/B tests of a medically reviewed knowledge graph. Agreeing with the client what a good answer looked like before building anything is the habit I would bring to client projects at Konrad.",

 r"At Ipsos Strategy3, I supported strategy projects by turning more than 80 expert interviews into quantitative insight and building market-sizing models, and I worked with the research and strategy teams to turn the findings into recommendations for clients. That is where I learned to present a finding to an audience who wants the implication rather than the method. My MSc dissertation, which used data from 458,840 UK Biobank participants and was delivered as an interactive Streamlit tool, strengthened my ability to make complex analysis usable for non-specialists.",

